  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="2e66-bd47-3c73-bd86" name="Later Macedonian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #29 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). 260 BC to 148 BC After the successor wars, Macedonia continued in possession of some elephants and the Successors list can still be used down to the commencement date for this list, which is intended to represent the state after the last elephants grew too old to be of military use. It covers the period down through the wars with, and eventual annexation by, the rising power of Rome. Allies: The army may have allied contingents from the Illyrian, Thracian and Galatian lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Later Macedonian]
  Cavalry: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  War Machines, Allies and Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 20% Infantry: At least 25% War Machines, Allies and Mercenaries: Up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
